## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/randomrgb.html
- Summary (EN): Random RGB generates random colours for an RGB layer, VDB or attribute. Colours come from Min/Max channel ranges, a colour ramp, or a palette of specific values, and colour derivation modes (complementary, analogous, triadic, tetradic, shades, tints) apply to Specific Values.
- Résumé (FR) : Ce nœud génère des couleurs aléatoires pour un calque RGB, à partir de plages, d'une rampe de couleurs ou d'une palette de valeurs.

- Inputs meaning: ["size_ref: representative layer that sets the output image size and metadata", "min: minimum component limit when Range Values is Min/Max", "max: maximum component limit when Range Values is Min/Max", "ramp: ramp sampled horizontally when Range Values is Color Ramp", "seed: controls the random colour distribution, allowing variation per custom shape"]

- Key parameters: ["Signature: layer type the node outputs", "Range Values: Min/Max, Color Ramp or Specific Values", "Color Model (Min/Max only): RGB constrains the red, green and blue ranges; HSV restricts hue, saturation and value to a slice of the colour wheel", "Relative to Color: base colour that small random deviations are applied around", "Red/Green/Blue and Hue/Saturation/Value Min/Max: range limits per component", "Color Ramp: maps the intermediate random value through a ramp to get the final colour", "Color Palette and Number of Colors (Specific Values only): preset palette filling the number of colours", "Color # modes: Constant, Complementary, 2 Analogous, 4 Analogous, Triadic, Tetradic, 5 Shades, 5 Tints", "Weight: how often each adjustment value is sampled; equal weights mean equal probability", "Angle and Distance: Angle sets the spacing around the colour wheel; Distance sets the brightness step for 5 Shades or the saturation step for 5 Tints", "Random per Pixel: selection varies per pixel for grain-like noise", "Seed and Time: both drive the randomness", "Zero Negative IDs: when a seed input is connected, outputs black where the seed is a negative integer"]

- Caveats: ["Per-pixel variation requires Random per Pixel to be enabled or a seed input to be wired; otherwise the fill is uniform across the layer.", "Min/max and ramp inputs apply only in their matching Range Values mode.", "Color Model applies only when Range Values is Min/Max.", "Zero Negative IDs has an effect only when a seed is connected.", "The page gives identical descriptions for Triadic and 2 Analogous, so the difference between them is unclear from this page alone."]

